{"id": 25, "ts": 1781183110.650573, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I agree with Sarah\u2019s provisional vote for Candidate\u202fB.\u202fHis documented conscientiousness, strong stress handling, solid technical competence (weather assessment, computer skills) and quick, accurate decision\u2011making align well with the core safety\u2011critical criteria for long\u2011distance flights.\u202fWhile his pretentious demeanor and occasional tone issues are concerning, they appear manageable through targeted coaching, and there is no evidence of deficits in attention or decision quality beyond the noted weak memory for numbers.\nTurning to Candidate\u202fD, we have clear strengths\u2014adequate response to unexpected events, excellent concentration, superior problem\u2011solving, and a serious sense of responsibility\u2014which are valuable for long\u2011haul operations.\u202fHowever, the concerns that he is \u201cmoody\u201d and regarded as a \u201cloner,\u201d combined with the lack of any observed data on his crew\u2011cooperation or professional communication (Sarah reports no specific observations), leave a critical gap in the evidence for the cooperation and communication criteria.\u202fWithout assurance that D can collaborate effectively in the cockpit, his technical strengths cannot outweigh the potential risk to crew dynamics.\nGiven the current evidence, I maintain my vote for **Candidate\u202fB**, while recommending we continue to probe Candidate\u202fD\u2019s teamwork and communication style before making a final decision."}
